      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-02-06T13:46:07.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Gene Bound Ion Lancers</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But, no. Those are not Gene Bound Ion Lancers. Those are the same unknowns&nbsp;<span>&nbsp;on&nbsp;</span><a href=\"http://sotm.wikidot.com/heroes:k-n-y-f-e\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">K.N.Y.F.E</a><span>'s Incidental Contact,&nbsp;</span><a href=\"http://sotm.wikidot.com/heroes:the-argent-adept\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">The Argent Adept</a><span>'s Syncopated Onslaught,&nbsp;</span><a href=\"http://sotm.wikidot.com/heroes:omnitron-x\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Omnitron-X</a><span>'s Defensive Blast,&nbsp;</span><a href=\"http://sotm.wikidot.com/heroes:the-visionary\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">The Visionary</a><span>'s Cerebral Hemorrhage.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Their armor is different than the Ion Lancer (Color, shape) they aren't showing their midrif's (as the ion lancers are) and their helms actually have a different shape - you can see a close up of an ion lancer helm on Expat's Unload, which is different than these guys.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>These guys are my now favorite 'Who are they!!' and I can't wait to see if their space armor like appearance leads them to show up in WotC</span></p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:13:53.627Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
